===Critical reception===
The third season received highly positive reviews, and is noteworthy for drawing in more critics for its exploration of [[artificial intelligence]], as well as its timely storytelling format. On [[Rotten Tomatoes]], the season has an approval rating of 100% and average rating of 7.7 out of 10 based on 11 reviews. The site's critical consensus is, "''Person of Interest'' weaves compelling standalone stories into its engrossing serial narrative, and incorporates welcome bursts of humor into its sci-fi mystery core."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/person-of-interest/s03/ |title=Person of Interest: Season 3 |publisher=Rotten Tomatoes |access-date=August 24, 2017}}</ref>

In regards to the season, ''[[Slant Magazine]]'' said that the show "is at its best when sticking to cutting-edge topics" and called it a "solid action-thriller that intersperses twist-filled standalone episodes into its season-long arcs."<ref>{{cite web|last=Riccio|first=Aaron|title=Person of Interest: Season 3|url=https://www.slantmagazine.com/tv/review/person-of-interest-season-three|work=Slant Magazine|date=October 17, 2013|access-date=September 20, 2014}}</ref> ''[[The A.V. Club]]'' said that the show captures the "national post-post-9/11 mood"<ref>{{cite web|last=Dyess-Nugent|first=Phil|title=How Person Of Interest captures the national post-post-9/11 mood|url=https://www.avclub.com/article/how-iperson-of-interest-icaptures-the-national-ipo-92502|work=The A.V. Club|date=February 14, 2013|access-date=September 20, 2014}}</ref> and that with the mid-season arc in season three, "turns conspiracy theory into art".<ref>{{cite web|last=Handlen|first=Zack|title=Person Of Interest turns conspiracy theory into art|url=https://www.avclub.com/review/person-of-interest-turns-conspiracy-theory-into-ar-200648|work=The A.V. Club|date=December 17, 2013|access-date=September 20, 2014}}</ref> 

The season's two story arcs both received a considerable amount of praise: the two episodes ending the HR storyline are commonly considered to be some of the best episodes of ''Person of Interest''. Matt Fowler of [[IGN]] gave "The Crossing" a 10 out of 10, reacting extremely positively to the cliffhanger at the ending.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2013/.../person-of-interest-the-crossing-review|title=Person of Interest: "The Crossing" Review|last=Fowler|first=Matt|work=IGN|date=November 20, 2013|access-date=February 19, 2015}}{{Dead link|date=September 2024 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> The episode to follow, "[[The Devil's Share]]", was the most acclaimed episode of the season, being praised for its opening sequence, its writing, [[Chris Fisher (director)|Chris Fisher]]'s direction, and the acting performances, especially those by Jim Caviezel and Kevin Chapman. Surette called the episode a "stunner" and declared it as the series' possible best episode, praising the opening sequence as the "greatest sequence the series ever put together", feeling it succeeded in eclipsing the devastation induced by Carter's death. Surette also praised Fusco's effectiveness and character development in the episode, as well naming the cinematography and direction to be the best of the series, and identifying points of symbolism in the episode he felt were noteworthy and effective.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tv.com/shows/person-of-interest-2011/community/post/person-of-interest-the-devils-share-review-season-3-episode-10-138549683486/|last=Surette|first=Tim|date=November 27, 2013|work=TV.com|title=Person of Interest "The Devil's Share" Review: Revenge, Redemption, and Resolution|access-date=November 26, 2014|archive-date=May 16, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170516104414/http://www.tv.com/shows/person-of-interest-2011/community/post/person-of-interest-the-devils-share-review-season-3-episode-10-138549683486/|url-status=dead}}</ref> Fowler gave the episode an "amazing" rating of a 9.3 out of 10, also praising the opening sequence, as well as the flashbacks and the ending scene.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2013/11/27/person-of-interest-the-devils-share-review|last=Fowler|first=Matt|title=Person of Interest: "The Devil's Share" Review|work=IGN|date=November 26, 2013|access-date=November 26, 2014}}</ref> Phil Dyess-Nugent of ''The A.V. Club'' gave the episode a perfect A rating, praising the atmosphere of grief the episode built and feeling Fusco's character development served as an appropriate tribute to Carter.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.avclub.com/person-of-interest-the-devils-share-1798178831|title=Person Of Interest: "The Devil's Share" Review|last=Dyess-Nugent|first=Phil|work=The A.V. Club|date=November 27, 2013|access-date=November 27, 2014}}</ref> Sean McKenna of ''TV Fanatic'' called the opening sequence "brilliant",<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tvfanatic.com/2013/11/person-of-interest-review-reeses-revenge/|last=McKenna|first=Sean|title=Person of Interest Review: Reese's Revenge|work=TV Fanatic|date=November 27, 2013|access-date=November 27, 2014}}</ref> while Courtney Vaudreuil of ''TV Equals'' praised the ending.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tvequals.com/2013/11/27/person-of-interest-season-3-review-the-devils-share/|title=Person of Interest Season 3 Review "The Devil's Share"|last=Vaudreuil|first=Courtney|work=TV Equals|date=November 27, 2013|access-date=November 27, 2014}}</ref>

